      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The first total synthesis of the phosphorylated trisaccharide repeating unit of Providencia alcalifaciens O22 is reported. The trisaccharide contains rare deoxyamino sugar AAT at the reducing end and d-glyceramide 2-phosphate at the other end. The efficient synthesis involves one-pot assembly of trisaccharide and late-stage phosphorylation as key steps."},
